event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":98,"item_id":"rs_004306223fad8498016ac956d7c8708195b59adfdff619e305","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Implementing server forms**\n\nI’m thinking about creating simple HTML forms for full navigation without needing an API. I’ll use native forms with POST redirects and ensure validation so that any 422 errors are clearly shown with an alert role. I want to set up a row div and work with SQLite. It’s important to run my tests with node’s HTTP spawn in temporary directories outside of the main directory, ensuring any test data gets cleaned up. And of course, I’ll add a README for clarity!"}

